  "reason": "Evidence: The top-3 experiments all use multimodal + multiprofile + imagenet_vit_l + transformer, with weighted fusion (config_029, 0.7250) slightly edging out concat (config_008, 0.7207). RNA-only (config_001, 0.6530) confirms multimodal is essential. The current best uses scvi_n200 as the RNA encoder, but no alternative RNA encoder has been tested in this strong multimodal setting. Question: config_010 swaps only the RNA encoder to scgpt while keeping imagenet_vit_l, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion fixed, directly testing whether a different RNA representation can push accuracy above 0.725. Why: With 6 experiments remaining, identifying the best RNA encoder in the proven multimodal/transformer/weighted pipeline is the highest-leverage single-variable exploration; it either confirms scvi_n200 is optimal (allowing exploitation of other axes) or reveals a new best encoder to build on."
}

